   269 				; vbxe_pb_write_big - Copy img_big_buf to VRAM page buffer, 16-bit count
   270 				; Input: img_chunk_lo/hi = byte count (preserved by vbxe_img_write_big)
   271 				; Used by http_download: page data arrives via fn_read_img in up-to-2KB
   272 				; SIO chunks (8x fewer SIO calls than the old 255-byte fn_read path).
   273 				; Loads page-buffer write state into the image write pointer, copies via
   274 				; the fast vbxe_img_write_big block routine, then stores the state back.
   275 				; Safe: page download and image fetch never run concurrently (dl_active).
   276 				; Plain RAM ops + jsr, so this proc itself has no below-$4000 requirement.
   277 				; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
